@title Cold Room B alarm
@subtitle Runbook for a temperature alarm at Marlowe Vaccine Depot
@author Depot Operations, Owner

kpi Safe range | 2–8 °C | Cold Room B
kpi Doses held | 12,400 | neutral
kpi Night supervisor | 555-0187 | Gabriela Nunez
kpi Quality Manager | 555-0152 | Peter Aldous

!!! Never discard any doses. Only the Quality Manager, Peter Aldous (555-0152), decides what happens to stock that was out of range.

# Alarm levels
table = level,trigger; Warning,Above 8 °C for 10 minutes; Critical,Above 12 °C or below 0 °C

# First 15 minutes
1. Acknowledge the alarm on the monitoring panel within 5 minutes.
2. Check that the door is fully shut and the seal is intact.
3. Check that the compressor has power, and note the temperature shown on the data logger.
4. Call the refrigeration contractor Polar Service on 555-0190. They respond within 4 hours.

# Moving stock
If the temperature is **still above 8 °C after 15 minutes**, move the stock out of Cold Room B.
table = destination,doses; Backup Cold Room C,"9,000"; 6 validated transport boxes with ice packs,"3,400"
- Log every box on the transfer sheet.

# Quarantine and escalation
- Any lot out of range for **more than 30 minutes in total** is quarantined.
- Tell the Quality Manager immediately.
- If the alarm is not resolved within **2 hours**, call the Operations Director.

!!! Do not discard anything, even if it looks spoiled. Quarantine it and wait for the Quality Manager's decision.

# Contacts
table = role,name,phone; Night supervisor,Gabriela Nunez,555-0187; Quality Manager,Peter Aldous,555-0152; Refrigeration contractor,Polar Service,555-0190
